title: December 2025

@collective_bargaining_2025
# prose-audit: Grade B — The enacted framework now belongs to the live labour minister, OPZZ, Solidarność, employers and procurement offices, with implementation and opposition authority kept distinct.
title: The collective-bargaining framework enters force
subtitle: A labour institution, not a one-time transfer
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 24
order: 20
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/poland/cards/labour-inspection.webp
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 12 and government_party != "pis" and caretaker_government = 0
on-arrival: collective_bargaining_framework_active = 1; labor_credibility += 4; union_trust += 2; opzz_cooperation += 2; labor_dissent -= 1; government_delivery += 3; news_headline = "A new framework can make sectoral bargaining real—or remain paper"

= December 2025 — Enforcement after enactment

The new law creates rules for registering and promoting collective agreements.
Labour Minister **[+ labor_minister +]** of **[+ labor_minister_party +]** now
faces the part no enactment photograph can perform: helping OPZZ, Solidarność
and other unions organise agreements that employers will sign and procurement
offices will reward.

[? if left_in_government: Lewica can fund registration support, organisers and
public-contract clauses from inside government.?][? if not left_in_government:
The ministry owns enforcement. Lewica can fund union support and expose weak
implementation, but it cannot spend the state reserve or command procurement.?]
The alternative is to claim a labour institution before it covers another
workplace.

- @bargaining_enforce
- @bargaining_claim

@bargaining_enforce
title: Negotiate implementation with OPZZ and the wider union movement
subtitle: Cost: 2 budget capacity in government, otherwise 2 resources.
choose-if: (left_in_government = 1 and budget >= 2) or (left_in_government = 0 and resources >= 2)
unavailable-subtitle: The framework has no implementation reserve.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.budget -= 2;
    Q.collective_bargaining_implementation = 2;
    Q.labor_credibility += 7;
    Q.union_trust += 9;
    Q.opzz_cooperation += 10;
    Q.labor_mobilization += 9;
    Q.labor_dissent -= 7;
    Q.workers_support += 5;
    Q.government_delivery += 4;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 2;
    Q.fiscal_stress += 1;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The bargaining statute receives institutions capable of using it";
} else {
    Q.resources -= 2;
    Q.collective_bargaining_implementation = 1;
    Q.labor_credibility += 5;
    Q.union_trust += 7;
    Q.opzz_cooperation += 7;
    Q.labor_mobilization += 8;
    Q.labor_dissent -= 5;
    Q.workers_support += 3;
    Q.local_network += 3;
    Q.news_headline =
        "Opposition unions build registration support while ministries control enforcement";
}
Q.razem_cooperation += 3;
Q.razem_dissent -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 2;
Q.spring_dissent -= 1;
Q.barons_dissent += 2;
!}

[? if left_in_government: Registration teams, procurement clauses and union
organisers receive funding together. Employers bidding for public work gain a
reason to bargain, and unions gain staff able to turn a legal framework into
sector agreements.?][? if not left_in_government: Lewica funds union advisers
and local registration support while publishing the enforcement the ministry
has not supplied. Workers gain organisational help; national procurement rules
remain outside our authority.?]

- @poland_event_queue: File the bargaining implementation plan

@bargaining_claim
title: Claim the statute and leave implementation to ministries
subtitle: Take credit for a real law before another workplace receives a collective agreement.
on-arrival: collective_bargaining_implementation = 0; media_capacity += 2; labor_credibility += 1; union_trust -= 6; opzz_cooperation -= 7; labor_dissent += 7; government_delivery += 1 if left_in_government = 1; public_trust -= 1; razem_dissent += 2; progressives_dissent += 1; news_headline = "The Left wins a labour headline while unions record an implementation breach"

Lewica tours studios with the enacted statute and leaves registration,
procurement and organising to existing ministries. The party receives some
credit for a genuine institutional reform. Union branches still waiting for an
agreement learn how little a framework changes when nobody funds its use.

- @poland_event_queue: Record the headline without enforcement

@left_leadership_2025
# prose-audit: Grade B — The primary result is strong, with seven distinct winners each given a real political meaning. The congress that reaches it is not: the premise is a two-line list of what the congress "can" do, with no delegates, venue or argument.
title: New Left chooses its post-merger leadership
subtitle: Earlier removal and the current caucus map determine who can stand
