@leader_primary_result
title: The membership primary chooses one chair
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
const leadershipCandidates = [
    {
        name: "Włodzimierz Czarzasty",
        key: "czarzasty",
        eligible: !Q.advisor_reshuffle_removed_czarzasty && Q.barons_active,
        score: (Number(Q.barons_strength) || 0) +
            (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) * 0.10 -
            (Number(Q.barons_dissent) || 0) * 0.15
    },
    {
        name: "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk",
        key: "dziemianowicz",
        eligible: Q.labor_active,
        score: (Number(Q.labor_parliamentary_influence) ||
            Number(Q.labor_strength) || 0) +
            (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) * 0.10 +
            (Number(Q.union_trust) || 0) * 0.06 +
            (Number(Q.workers_support) || 0) * 0.05 -
            (Number(Q.labor_conflict) ||
                Number(Q.labor_dissent) || 0) * 0.12
    },
    {
        name: "Krzysztof Gawkowski",
        key: "gawkowski",
        eligible: true,
        score: Q.progressives_active
            ? (Number(Q.progressives_strength) || 0) +
            (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) * 0.08 +
            (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) * 0.05 -
            (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) * 0.12
            : 0
    },
    {
        name: "Magdalena Biejat",
        key: "biejat",
        eligible: Q.razem_active && Q.razem_in_left,
        score: (Number(Q.labor_parliamentary_influence) ||
            Number(Q.labor_strength) || 0) * 0.65 +
            (Number(Q.union_trust) || 0) * 0.04 +
            (Number(Q.workers_support) || 0) * 0.20 +
            (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) * 0.10 -
            (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) * 0.12
    },
    {
        name: "Adrian Zandberg",
        key: "zandberg",
        eligible: Q.razem_active && Q.razem_in_left &&
            Q.razem_leader == "Adrian Zandberg" &&
            !Q.advisor_reshuffle_removed_zandberg,
        score: (Number(Q.razem_strength) || 0) +
            (Number(Q.razem_cooperation) || 0) * 0.10 -
            (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) * 0.15
    },
    {
        name: "Anna-Maria Żukowska",
        key: "zukowska",
        eligible: Q.progressives_active,
        score: (Number(Q.progressives_strength) || 0) +
            (Number(Q.progressive_credibility) || 0) * 0.12 +
            (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) * 0.06 -
            (Number(Q.progressives_dissent) || 0) * 0.10
    },
    {
        name: "Paulina Matysiak",
        key: "matysiak",
        eligible: Q.social_patriot_leader == "Paulina Matysiak" &&
            Q.matysiak_party == "Lewica Patriotyczna",
        score: (Number(Q.social_patriot_strength) || 0) +
            (Number(Q.social_patriot_local_organisation) || 0) * 0.08 +
            (Number(Q.rural_support) || 0) * 0.05 -
            (Number(Q.social_patriot_dissent) || 0) * 0.12
    }
].filter(function(candidate) {
    return candidate.eligible && candidate.name != Q.president_name;
});
if (!leadershipCandidates.length) {
    leadershipCandidates.push({
        name: "Krzysztof Gawkowski", key: "gawkowski", score: 0
    });
}
leadershipCandidates.sort(function(a, b) {
    if (b.score != a.score) return b.score - a.score;
    return a.name < b.name ? -1 : 1;
});
const winner = leadershipCandidates[0];
Q.left_primary_czarzasty_score = Math.round(
    (leadershipCandidates.find(function(candidate) {
        return candidate.key == "czarzasty";
    }) || {score: 0}).score * 10
) / 10;
Q.left_primary_dziemianowicz_score = Math.round(
    (leadershipCandidates.find(function(candidate) {
        return candidate.key == "dziemianowicz";
    }) || {score: 0}).score * 10
) / 10;
Q.left_primary_gawkowski_score = Math.round(
    (leadershipCandidates.find(function(candidate) {
        return candidate.key == "gawkowski";
    }) || {score: 0}).score * 10
) / 10;
Q.left_primary_matysiak_score = Math.round(
    (leadershipCandidates.find(function(candidate) {
        return candidate.key == "matysiak";
    }) || {score: 0}).score * 10
) / 10;
Q.left_primary_winner = winner.name;
Q.left_leader = winner.name;
Q.left_leadership_result = winner.name + " won the membership primary";
if (winner.key == "czarzasty") {
    Q.barons_strength += 2;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 2;
} else if (winner.key == "dziemianowicz") {
    Q.labor_strength += 4;
    Q.workers_support += 2;
} else if (winner.key == "gawkowski") {
    Q.progressives_strength += 4;
    Q.media_capacity += 2;
} else if (winner.key == "biejat") {
    Q.labor_strength += 3;
    Q.workers_support += 3;
    Q.razem_cooperation += 2;
} else if (winner.key == "zandberg") {
    Q.razem_strength += 4;
    Q.razem_cooperation += 3;
    Q.razem_dissent = Math.max(0, (Number(Q.razem_dissent) || 0) - 3);
} else if (winner.key == "zukowska") {
    Q.progressives_strength += 4;
    Q.progressive_credibility += 3;
    Q.media_capacity += 2;
} else {
    Q.social_patriot_strength += 4;
    Q.rural_support += 2;
}
Q.news_headline = winner.name + " wins the New Left membership primary";
!}

The members choose **[+ left_primary_winner +]**. A sitting President—**[+
president_name +]**—was not eligible to turn the presidency into a party
chairmanship.

[? if left_primary_winner = "Włodzimierz Czarzasty": The old machine proves it
can still win an open electorate, giving Czarzasty a mandate stronger than an
executive arrangement. Progressives accept the ballot and begin organising for
the next one.?]
[? if left_primary_winner = "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": Dziemianowicz-Bąk
turns her parliamentary record and workplace credibility into a personal
mandate from party members. Lewica Pracy and union organisers strengthen that
mandate without becoming a separate party current.?]
[? if left_primary_winner = "Krzysztof Gawkowski": Gawkowski's progressive
and media network wins the open contest. Labour and the old machine now bargain
with a chair whose authority came from neither founder's protected half.?]
[? if left_primary_winner = "Magdalena Biejat": Biejat turns Razem's social
and housing credibility into a common-party chairmanship. Her mandate keeps
the party's welfare language visible while making its parliamentary work more
legible to the wider Left.?]
[? if left_primary_winner = "Adrian Zandberg": Zandberg carries Razem's
opposition-left programme into the common party. The congress accepts a chair
whose authority comes from the live Razem organisation rather than a merger
settlement.?]
[? if left_primary_winner = "Anna-Maria Żukowska": Żukowska's progressive
wing wins the chair and turns media discipline into a programme mandate. The
old machine, Lewica Pracy MPs and union organisers must now negotiate with a
sharper public voice.?]
[? if left_primary_winner = "Paulina Matysiak": Lewica Patriotyczna supplies
the winning organisation and the common party adopts a developmental,
welfare-sovereignty centre under Matysiak.?]

- @leader_primary_finish

@leader_primary_finish
title: Record the sole chair
go-to: poland_event_queue


@criminal_group_probe_2025
# prose-audit: Grade C — The constitutional stakes of a criminal investigation into a serving cabinet are set out with three real answers; the prosecutors on both sides of the case remain institutional roles.
title: A criminal investigation into the government itself
subtitle: Prosecutors examine whether ministers acted as an organised group
face-image: img/poland/events/supreme-court.webp
new-page: true
tags: poland_event
priority: 30
order: 12
max-visits: 1
view-if: continuous_campaign = 1 and year = 2025 and month = 12 and criminal_group_probe_2025_done = 0 and government_party != "pis" and pres_2025_hostile_president = 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.criminal_group_probe_2025_done = 1;
Q.constitutional_conflict_level =
    (Number(Q.constitutional_conflict_level) || 0) + 20;
Q.prosecution_independence = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.prosecution_independence) || 0) - 6
);
Q.institutional_trust = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.institutional_trust) || 0) - 5
);
Q.news_headline =
    "Prosecutors open a file naming serving ministers as an organised group";
!}

= December 2025 — The charge that has no ordinary answer

A prosecutorial file is opened on a notification alleging that the Prime
Minister and senior ministers acted as an organised criminal group in taking
control of the prosecution service, the public media and the state companies —
described in the notification as a coup against the constitutional order.

This is not opposition rhetoric with a legal costume. A notification obliges
prosecutors to act, the prosecution service is itself the object of the
dispute, and the Palace has an interest in the outcome. Whatever the file
contains, the state has now produced a document in which its own government is
a suspect and its own courts are the venue.

There is no institutionally clean response. Ignoring it concedes that a
criminal file against a serving cabinet is normal. Suppressing it proves the
charge. Answering it in substance accepts that a prosecutor decides which
government is lawful.

[? if surveillance_scandal_stage >= 2: We have already lived through one
argument about services being turned on the other camp, and both sides took
away the lesson that it works.?]
[? if szmydt_response = "Clearance review": The clearance review we forced in
2024 is the reason several of the officials now handling this file were vetted
at all, and it is being cited by both sides.?]
[? if left_in_government = 1: Our own ministers are inside the perimeter of
the notification, whether or not they are named in it.?][? if
left_in_government = 0: We are outside the cabinet, which lets us defend the
constitutional point
without defending every decision that produced it.?]

- @probe_procedural
- @probe_political
- @probe_counter

@probe_procedural
title: Insist the file runs its ordinary course, publicly and without interference
subtitle: The only answer that does not concede the premise; it leaves a criminal file open over the cabinet for months.
on-arrival: constitutional_restraint += 8; prosecution_independence += 8; judicial_legitimacy += 4; institutional_trust += 5; public_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum -= 0.1; constitutional_conflict_level -= 6; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 9; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 7; news_headline = "The coalition lets the file proceed and refuses to touch it"

No minister comments on the case, no instruction reaches a prosecutor, and the
file proceeds exactly as any other would. The dates and the decisions are
published so that interference would be visible if it occurred.

The cost is real and unavoidable: for as long as the file is open, every
foreign partner and every domestic institution deals with a government under
criminal examination. We have decided that this is less dangerous than a
government that decides which files exist.

- @poland_event_queue: Let the file proceed

@probe_political
title: Name it publicly as an attempted constitutional coup by prosecution
subtitle: Correct in substance and it escalates a legal conflict into an open question about who governs.
on-arrival: constitutional_conflict_level += 15; prosecution_independence -= 5; institutional_trust -= 4; public_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; pis_relation -= 10; president_relation -= 8; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += -8; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 12; news_headline = "The government calls the criminal file an attempt to remove it by prosecution"

We say what it is: an attempt to settle by criminal procedure a question that
belongs to the Sejm and the electorate. Our supporters need to hear it and
much of the country agrees.

From this point there are two publicly declared coups in Polish politics and
each side has named the other. Neither institution involved can now act
without being read as a participant, and every subsequent prosecutorial
decision is received as a move in a war.

- @poland_event_queue: Name the file publicly

@probe_counter
title: Legislate a clear procedure for investigating serving ministers
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Builds the missing rule instead of winning the argument; the President will almost certainly veto it.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no legislative capacity to draft a ministerial-liability procedure.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; constitutional_restraint += 6; prosecution_command_clarity += 8; institutional_trust += 5; administrative_reform_pressure += 3; president_relation -= 4; president_veto_count += 1; public_trust += 2; news_headline = "A ministerial-liability procedure is tabled and sent towards a certain veto"

The gap is genuine: Poland has a Tribunal of State that nobody uses and no
workable rule for what an ordinary prosecutor may do with a serving minister.
We write one, applying to every future cabinet including our opponents'.

The Palace vetoes it, as everyone in the chamber expected when it was tabled.
The text survives the veto and will be picked up by whoever next discovers, in
government, that this hole is still open.

- @poland_event_queue: Table the liability procedure
